---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Explicitly evaluate an authored probe or generate native artifacts from its isolated unit

Usage: pse compiler probe [OPTIONS] --question <QUESTION> <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>

Options:
  -C <checkout>
      --kind <KIND>              [default: evaluate] [possible values: mir, facts, thir, type-sizes, mono-items, evaluate]
      --format <FORMAT>          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --question <QUESTION>      Original constant/layout/ownership/instance question; authored source owns stdout meaning
      --body <BODY>
      --fields <FIELDS>          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices
      --budget <BUDGET>          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --fact-focus <FACT_FOCUS>  Native query family for typed facts [default: all] [possible values: all, captures, suspension, cleanup]
      --pass <PASSES>
  -h, --help                     Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Explicitly evaluate an authored probe or generate native artifacts from its isolated unit

Usage: pse compiler probe [OPTIONS] --question <QUESTION> <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>


Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --kind <KIND>
          Possible values:
          - mir:        Body/pass-filtered MIR before/after files
          - facts:      Owned typed capture, suspension and cleanup observations from the pinned compiler
          - thir:       Selected unit THIR debug text; native rustc has no body filter for this view
          - type-sizes: Selected unit encountered concrete layouts; no cross-target ABI conclusion
          - mono-items: Selected unit monomorphization collection, separate from runtime reach
          - evaluate:   Authored isolated probe evaluation; stdout meaning belongs to its source

          [default: evaluate]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --question <QUESTION>
          Original constant/layout/ownership/instance question; authored source owns stdout meaning

      --body <BODY>


      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --fact-focus <FACT_FOCUS>
          Native query family for typed facts

          Possible values:
          - all:        Acquire all supported families within the selected owning body
          - captures:   Capture places, types, modes and source causes
          - suspension: Saved coroutine fields and their suspension variants
          - cleanup:    Analysis initialization and lowered normal/unwind cleanup

          [default: all]

      --pass <PASSES>


  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
